{"id":"m2://rec/open_logic/content/intuitionistic-logic/semantics/semantic-notions.tex#defn:restrict#1","source":"open_logic","snapshot":"blake3:a5eb116529d3e799289dd9f7e7530d0d446b3615f5608fe08c668241eee3c765","locator":"https://github.com/OpenLogicProject/OpenLogic/blob/1e960beff9ed7835bf3e3f1335e21af3439cd107/content/intuitionistic-logic/semantics/semantic-notions.tex#L42","native_id":"content/intuitionistic-logic/semantics/semantic-notions.tex#defn:restrict","kind":"definition","text":"Suppose $\\mModel{M}$ is a relational model and $w \\in W$. The\n  \\emph{restriction} $\\mModel{M}_w=\\tuple{W_w, R_w, V_w}$\n  of~$\\mModel{M}$ to~$w$ is given by:\n  \\begin{align*}\n    W_w & = \\Setabs{u \\in W}{Rwu},\\\\\n    R_w  & = R \\cap (W_w)^2, \\text{ and}\\\\\n    V_w(p) & = V(p) \\cap W_w.\n  \\end{align*}","class":"open","by":"textbook/1","resource":"PKGMM3P5QY","at":{"section":"32.6","kind":"defn"}}
